1
00:00:03,916 --> 00:00:04,916
Lin Zai.

2
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:16,625
Lin Zai.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Sister Chen!

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Sister Chen.

5
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:34,208
Lin Zai.

6
00:00:34,791 --> 00:00:35,791
It really is you.

7
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:39,208
Li Ming, he...

8
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:40,125
He...

9
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:41,125
I know.

10
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:42,333
Save your breath.

11
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:43,083
Save your strength.

12
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:44,083
We're taking you home.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,500
Okay.

14
00:00:46,791 --> 00:00:47,791
Let me help.

15
00:00:48,041 --> 00:00:49,583
It's fine, I can manage.

16
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,125
A-Leh, what are you doing?

17
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:04,368
She has a wound on her waist.

18
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,833
We can't rule out a bite.

19
00:01:08,875 --> 00:01:09,875
No, it's not.

20
00:01:10,083 --> 00:01:11,883
That happened when I
was running for my life.

21
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:13,458
I fell.

22
00:01:13,708 --> 00:01:14,750
Or maybe I got scratched.

23
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:16,166
I...

24
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:17,500
I can't remember.

25
00:01:18,833 --> 00:01:19,833
You can't remember?

26
00:01:22,625 --> 00:01:23,625
A-Leh.

27
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:24,708
She's Sister Chen.

28
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:25,791
She wouldn't lie to us.

29
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:34,953
Let's check her temperature.

30
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,125
Better safe than sorry.

31
00:01:52,375 --> 00:01:53,375
Lin Zai.

32
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:16,500
"The Last Oath"

33
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:21,400
(Episode 15: Dao Camp)

34
00:03:41,625 --> 00:03:43,291
Help! Is anyone there?

35
00:03:44,958 --> 00:03:46,038
We've got a wounded person!

36
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:53,958
When did she get hurt?

37
00:03:54,916 --> 00:03:56,333
It's fine, just a scratch.

38
00:03:57,375 --> 00:03:59,499
Don't move, the wound is deep.

39
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,620
Why didn't you say anything?

40
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:03,000
Come on, let's get you patched up.

41
00:04:16,625 --> 00:04:18,791
Here, have some water.

42
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,500
Here, Grandma.

43
00:06:08,125 --> 00:06:09,625
Sister Chen, Sister Chen.

44
00:06:30,041 --> 00:06:31,416
Li Ming, he...

45
00:07:06,868 --> 00:07:08,548
Looks like Brother Li was craving a drink.

46
00:07:10,458 --> 00:07:11,458
Brother Li.

47
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:14,208
The liquor you love,

48
00:07:14,916 --> 00:07:16,041
I brought it for you.

49
00:07:21,583 --> 00:07:22,583
Rest in peace.

50
00:07:30,041 --> 00:07:31,041
Oh, Li Ming.

51
00:07:32,916 --> 00:07:34,375
Go in peace.

52
00:07:37,791 --> 00:07:39,166
Chen Jin is fine.

53
00:07:42,083 --> 00:07:44,375
Lin Zai is back too.

54
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
We are...

55
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:52,375
All doing well.

56
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,750
Don't cry, Grandma.

57
00:08:13,708 --> 00:08:14,958
These past couple of days,

58
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:17,000
I've been thinking.

59
00:08:18,416 --> 00:08:20,166
This camp...

60
00:08:20,916 --> 00:08:22,666
Let's just stay here.

61
00:08:24,625 --> 00:08:26,385
Brother Dao and his
people are kind-hearted.

62
00:08:26,916 --> 00:08:28,458
With everyone together,

63
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:29,875
It's peaceful.

64
00:08:32,541 --> 00:08:33,583
From now on,

65
00:08:34,291 --> 00:08:35,875
The three of us can stay together,

66
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:39,125
And look out for each other.

67
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:42,750
Sure, this place...

68
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:44,416
is pretty nice.

69
00:08:47,083 --> 00:08:48,083
Lin Zai.

70
00:08:48,375 --> 00:08:49,625
What do you think?

71
00:09:33,041 --> 00:09:34,041
Lin Zai.

72
00:09:34,583 --> 00:09:35,750
Let's talk.

73
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:39,250
I'm not in the mood right now.

74
00:09:41,916 --> 00:09:42,916
Brother Li is gone.

75
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,750
Sister Chen hasn't recovered yet.

76
00:09:46,666 --> 00:09:48,506
And Grandma needs
someone to take care of her.

77
00:09:50,666 --> 00:09:52,750
I can't let anything else happen to them.

78
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:58,333
I understand all of that.

79
00:09:59,375 --> 00:10:01,000
But that shouldn't stop us from talking.

80
00:10:04,833 --> 00:10:05,833
A-Leh.

81
00:10:06,875 --> 00:10:08,166
My mind is a mess right now.

82
00:10:09,250 --> 00:10:10,416
I have nothing to talk about.

83
00:10:55,666 --> 00:10:56,666
You're here.

84
00:10:57,333 --> 00:10:58,916
Chen Jin just fell asleep.

85
00:11:01,375 --> 00:11:04,000
Thank goodness you and
A-Leh brought her back.

86
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:09,208
Come sit with Grandma for a bit.

87
00:11:22,541 --> 00:11:25,000
I haven't had the chance to ask you.

88
00:11:25,791 --> 00:11:26,833
You and A-Leh...

89
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:29,041
How did you find this place?

90
00:11:36,791 --> 00:11:38,291
Actually, I was taken by him.

91
00:11:42,666 --> 00:11:45,208
That day we went
looking for wild berries...

92
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,333
He forced me out of the camp.

93
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:50,625
Why would he do that?

94
00:11:52,875 --> 00:11:53,916
Is he a bad guy?

95
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:56,708
Grandma, he's not a bad guy.

96
00:11:57,583 --> 00:11:59,291
Even though when we first hit the road,

97
00:11:59,416 --> 00:12:00,696
It was because he had a mission.

98
00:12:01,666 --> 00:12:03,291
But along the way,

99
00:12:04,083 --> 00:12:05,083
He saved me,

100
00:12:05,625 --> 00:12:06,625
protected me,

101
00:12:07,416 --> 00:12:08,750
and taught me how to use a bow.

102
00:12:10,958 --> 00:12:12,250
He's been really good to me.

103
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:16,833
Sometimes I even forget that he kidnapped me.

104
00:12:18,208 --> 00:12:20,166
Then where is he taking you?

105
00:12:22,291 --> 00:12:22,791
Grandma.

106
00:12:23,291 --> 00:12:24,916
I can't tell you that right now.

107
00:12:29,416 --> 00:12:30,999
If you don't want to go with him,

108
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,333
I'll go talk to Brother Dao.

109
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:35,666
It's not really that.

110
00:12:36,166 --> 00:12:40,589
I just haven't figured out how I
should move forward with him.

111
00:12:41,583 --> 00:12:42,958
Then you should stay.

112
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:45,125
We can live a good life here ourselves.

113
00:12:45,916 --> 00:12:47,124
I do want to stay.

114
00:12:47,125 --> 00:12:48,208
But A-Leh...

115
00:12:53,708 --> 00:12:54,708
Child.

116
00:12:55,041 --> 00:12:56,665
If you haven't made up your mind yet,

117
00:12:56,666 --> 00:12:58,166
take your time to think about it.

118
00:12:59,208 --> 00:13:00,208
But,

119
00:13:00,723 --> 00:13:05,576
no matter what, always remember
to put your own feelings first.

120
00:13:14,458 --> 00:13:15,458
Lin Zai.

121
00:13:16,291 --> 00:13:17,771
Have you really thought this through?

122
00:13:18,083 --> 00:13:20,000
To love a human weapon?

123
00:13:41,208 --> 00:13:42,458
Just kill me.

124
00:13:44,583 --> 00:13:48,708
While I still have some humanity left.

125
00:13:57,708 --> 00:13:59,166
Look closely.

126
00:14:01,250 --> 00:14:03,291
I'm a monster who needs to drink blood.

127
00:14:04,208 --> 00:14:06,375
Just to stay sane.

128
00:14:09,416 --> 00:14:10,416
Changhuan.

129
00:14:22,041 --> 00:14:23,791
What's the point of you doing all this?

130
00:14:26,958 --> 00:14:28,666
You don't owe our family anything.

131
00:14:31,125 --> 00:14:32,125
Let me go,

132
00:14:32,703 --> 00:14:33,869
or kill me.

133
00:14:34,416 --> 00:14:35,416
Either is fine.

134
00:14:35,916 --> 00:14:37,125
I'm begging you.

135
00:14:43,125 --> 00:14:44,365
It's not about repaying a debt.

136
00:14:47,166 --> 00:14:48,333
I want to save you.

137
00:14:50,166 --> 00:14:52,000
It's never been for any other reason.

138
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:55,166
It's simply because it's you.

139
00:15:18,166 --> 00:15:19,375
Who the hell are you?

140
00:15:19,541 --> 00:15:20,541
What do you want?

141
00:15:20,666 --> 00:15:21,832
Mind your own damn business!

142
00:15:21,833 --> 00:15:22,993
What's that supposed to mean?

143
00:15:25,291 --> 00:15:26,291
Damn it.

144
00:16:08,958 --> 00:16:10,916
I want sweet and sour ribs today.

145
00:16:13,291 --> 00:16:14,291
Yao.

146
00:16:14,375 --> 00:16:15,455
What happened to your head?

147
00:16:15,791 --> 00:16:19,000
You only knew I came home a
few minutes late, looking like a mess.

148
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,165
Mom gave me all her attention.

149
00:16:21,166 --> 00:16:22,166
I accidentally fell.

150
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:25,500
But when I saw you come
home safely, at that moment,

151
00:16:28,416 --> 00:16:30,458
the beating I took didn't matter anymore.

152
00:16:32,375 --> 00:16:33,875
As long as I could protect you,

153
00:16:35,146 --> 00:16:36,426
it was worth more than anything.

154
00:16:44,708 --> 00:16:46,333
Everything I've done...

155
00:16:47,708 --> 00:16:50,398
has never been about gratitude or responsibility.

156
00:16:51,333 --> 00:16:52,333
Then...

157
00:16:53,791 --> 00:16:55,166
Then what is it for?

158
00:17:19,791 --> 00:17:21,333
You always wanted to beat me before.

159
00:17:23,708 --> 00:17:25,041
But to me,

160
00:17:28,208 --> 00:17:29,208
all I cared about.

161
00:17:30,458 --> 00:17:32,041
was after you beat me,

162
00:17:33,041 --> 00:17:34,291
the way your eyes lit up...

163
00:17:34,889 --> 00:17:36,556
When you came running to show off,

164
00:17:38,855 --> 00:17:40,271
when you faced a tough problem,

165
00:17:41,583 --> 00:17:43,543
the way you'd bite your
pen, refusing to give up...

166
00:17:48,916 --> 00:17:50,416
It's always been because of you.

167
00:17:53,083 --> 00:17:54,625
Shen Changhuan, you...

168
00:17:58,083 --> 00:17:59,083
Are you saying...

169
00:18:00,833 --> 00:18:01,999
what I think you're saying?

170
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Yes.

171
00:18:06,708 --> 00:18:07,708
I...

172
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:08,833
I...

173
00:18:10,625 --> 00:18:12,166
I always thought...

174
00:18:13,291 --> 00:18:14,708
you didn't feel that way.

175
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:18,166
So I was really frustrated.

176
00:18:20,166 --> 00:18:21,166
Why...

177
00:18:22,125 --> 00:18:24,041
Why was I always the one drawn to you,

178
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:26,333
while you...

179
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:28,874
while you never showed any sign of it?

180
00:18:28,875 --> 00:18:30,666
How could I show it?

181
00:18:33,250 --> 00:18:34,458
I was living under your roof.

182
00:18:35,291 --> 00:18:36,582
Your parents were so kind to me.

183
00:18:36,583 --> 00:18:37,903
And yet I had feelings for you...

184
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,500
How could I have the nerve?

185
00:18:55,291 --> 00:18:56,708
But now,

186
00:18:59,375 --> 00:19:01,000
I'm just a monster.

187
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,250
Changhuan.

188
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:16,375
You're not a monster.

189
00:19:20,041 --> 00:19:21,500
I'm going to turn you back into...

190
00:19:23,576 --> 00:19:25,326
that shining Shen Changhuan.

191
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,583
Where did you go?

192
00:20:47,916 --> 00:20:49,059
I just went to the cafeteria.

193
00:20:49,083 --> 00:20:51,123
I was afraid the food
would be gone if I went late.

194
00:20:52,041 --> 00:20:53,708
It's okay, I'm not hungry.

195
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:56,000
Give it to Grandma Qiu and the others.

196
00:20:57,458 --> 00:20:58,458
Grandma Qiu.

197
00:21:00,625 --> 00:21:02,000
He Yao, what are you doing?
